# === Clean-room RE: nothing copyrighted or owner-identifying enters git ===

# Vendor software working dirs (convention B: version-tracked desktop apps)
triage/
processed/

# Local vendor reference material (convention A): manuals, datasheets, scratch.
# NOTE: in this convention `docs/` is NOT tracked. Tracked findings live in the
# per-target folder (e.g. gm600/). Re-fetch reference material per machine; list
# source URLs in CLAUDE.md. Delete this line if your repo tracks docs/ instead.
docs/

# Image backups — codeplug/EEPROM/flash dumps, golden images. Still the vendor's
# content, and may contain the owner's serial numbers / PII.
*_backups/
**/flash_backups/
**/codeplug_backups/
*.golden

# Vendor binaries that might land at the repo root by accident
*.exe
*.dll
*.bin
*.cab
*.msi

# Vendor codeplug / config / firmware formats (decoded copies are still theirs)
*.cps
*.cpg
*.rcdx
*.rdb
*.rad
*.per
*.net
*.srec
*.mot

# Reverse-engineering tool databases (built from their binary)
*.idb
*.i64
*.id0
*.id1
*.id2
*.nam
*.til

# Host-specific agent notes (access, lab-PC paths, keys)
CLAUDE.local.md

# Build / sim / tool run artifacts
*.vcd
build/
dist/
node_modules/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
/venv

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
